---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CONFIG } from "../lib/config.js";

const year = new Date().getFullYear();

const hasEmail = Boolean(CONFIG.CONTACT_EMAIL);
const hasPhone = Boolean(CONFIG.CONTACT_PHONE);
const telHref = hasPhone ? `tel:${CONFIG.CONTACT_PHONE.replace(/[^0-9+]/g, "")}` : "";
---

<Layout
  title="FixTheHead — Nefesh Discovery & One-on-One Coaching"
  description="Suffer less, live more. One-on-one spiritual coaching and Nefesh Discovery sessions to help you see the options available on your path."
>
  <header>
    <nav class="wrap">
      <a class="brand" href="#top">FixTheHead</a>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#about">My Journey</a></li>
        <li><a href="#nefesh">Nefesh Discovery</a></li>
        <li><a href="#modalities">Modalities</a></li>
        <li><a href="#session">Sessions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#booking" class="nav-cta">Book Now</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h1>Suffer less. See more of what's possible.</h1>
        <p class="tagline">
          FixTheHead is a space for Nefesh Discovery — one-on-one work to help
          you find the options already available to you on the path toward a
          fuller, lighter life.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#booking">Book a Session</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#about">My Story</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="about">
      <div class="wrap two-col about-grid">
        <div class="portrait-frame">
          <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/images/moshe.png`} alt="Yanky" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">My Journey</div>
          <h2>Hi, I'm Yanky</h2>
          <p><em>(But that's just a name.)</em></p>
          <p>
            If my parents hadn't named me, who would I be? How would I even
            introduce myself? That exact question—"Who am I?"—is at the heart
            of how I help people fix their head.
          </p>
          <p>
            To get to this point, trust me, I've left no stone unturned. If
            there's a modality out there, I've probably tried it, bought the
            book, or sat on a floor somewhere doing it.
          </p>
          <p>
            I've read hundreds of books, listened to hundreds of podcasts,
            and spent quality time with traditional methods like CBT, DBT,
            IFS, ACT, somatic experiencing, and EMDR. I've sat through
            mindfulness retreats, breathwork sessions, and sound baths. I've
            chased gurus and Rebbes, taken psychedelic journeys, and let
            energy healers tap on my meridian points, wave crystals, and
            realign my aura until I wasn't sure if I was coming or going.
          </p>
          <p>
            While every single one of those tools offered real value and
            helped me along the way, I eventually realized something
            fundamental:
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>
              The simple, deep exploration of "Who am I?" is the single most
              powerful tool there is.
            </strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            It disintegrates the ego-driven stories and mental programming
            that keep us trapped inside our own heads, blocking us from
            actually enjoying life. It clears away the heavy noise so we can
            finally digest a simple truth: the Creator created us out of
            love, purely to give us the deepest pleasures of living.
          </p>
          <p>
            Because of everything I've walked through, I'm not here to push a
            rigid, one-size-fits-all formula on you. Instead, I can share
            what I genuinely believe will be the best path forward for your
            specific journey—including the tailored work we'll do together
            in our sessions.
          </p>
          <p>
            My goal is for you to walk away feeling empowered, educated, and
            ready to stop surviving inside your head and start enjoying
            life.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="explore">
      <div class="wrap explore-cta">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="kicker">Take the Next Step</div>
          <h2>Ready to Explore?</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Reach out to schedule your Nefesh Discovery session. Together,
          we'll cut through the inner noise, untangle the mind, and get you
          back to living fully.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#booking">Book Your Nefesh Discovery Session</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="nefesh" class="alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="kicker">The Work</div>
          <h2>What is Nefesh Discovery?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <p>
              <em>Nefesh</em> is a Hebrew word for the soul, or life-force —
              the part of you that's still asking questions underneath
              whatever is hurting right now.
            </p>
            <p>
              Nefesh Discovery is a guided process, not a fixed program.
              Together we slow down enough to see the options that are
              actually available to you on your path — the ones that get
              hidden by pain, habit, or old stories about who you have to be.
            </p>
            <p>
              The goal isn't to hand you a single answer. It's to help you
              recognize your own options clearly enough that you can choose
              one, and suffer a little less along the way.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="placeholder">
              Optional: add a short pull-quote or a specific example here of
              what a Nefesh Discovery session actually looks like in
              practice.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="modalities">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="kicker">Tools I Draw On</div>
          <h2>Modalities</h2>
          <p class="placeholder">
            The cards below are placeholders. Replace each title/description
            with the modalities you've personally experienced and now use with
            clients (e.g. breathwork, meditation, somatic practices, plant
            medicine integration, sound healing, shadow work, etc.).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="modalities-grid">
          <div class="modality-card">
            <h3 class="placeholder">Modality One</h3>
            <p class="placeholder">One or two sentences on what this is and how you use it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="modality-card">
            <h3 class="placeholder">Modality Two</h3>
            <p class="placeholder">One or two sentences on what this is and how you use it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="modality-card">
            <h3 class="placeholder">Modality Three</h3>
            <p class="placeholder">One or two sentences on what this is and how you use it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="modality-card">
            <h3 class="placeholder">Modality Four</h3>
            <p class="placeholder">One or two sentences on what this is and how you use it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="session" class="alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="kicker">Work With Me</div>
          <h2>One-on-One Session</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="session-card">
          <p>A focused, private Nefesh Discovery session — just the two of us.</p>
          <div class="price">$180 / 90 min</div>
          <ul class="session-includes">
            <li class="placeholder">What's included, point one</li>
            <li class="placeholder">What's included, point two</li>
            <li class="placeholder">What's included, point three</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#booking">Book Your Session</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="booking">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="kicker">Ready When You Are</div>
          <h2>Book &amp; Pay</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="booking-grid">
          <div class="calendar-embed">
            {CONFIG.CALENDLY_URL ? (
              <iframe
                src={CONFIG.CALENDLY_URL}
                style="width: 100%; height: 480px; border: none;"
                title="Book a session"
              />
            ) : (
              <div>
                <p><strong>Online scheduling is coming soon.</strong></p>
                <p>
                  For now, reach out directly to book your session:{" "}
                  {hasEmail ? (
                    <a href={`mailto:${CONFIG.CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONFIG.CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
                  ) : (
                    <span class="placeholder">add your email in src/lib/config.js</span>
                  )}
                </p>
              </div>
            )}
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="pay-card">
              <h3>Pay by Credit Card</h3>
              {CONFIG.STRIPE_PAYMENT_LINK ? (
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CONFIG.STRIPE_PAYMENT_LINK} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                  Pay by Credit Card
                </a>
              ) : (
                <span class="placeholder">
                  Stripe payment link coming soon — add STRIPE_PAYMENT_LINK in src/lib/config.js
                </span>
              )}
            </div>
            <div class="pay-card">
              <h3>Pay by Zelle</h3>
              {CONFIG.ZELLE_RECIPIENT ? (
                <p>
                  Send your Zelle payment to:<br />
                  <strong>{CONFIG.ZELLE_RECIPIENT}</strong>
                </p>
              ) : (
                <span class="placeholder">
                  Zelle email/phone coming soon — add ZELLE_RECIPIENT in src/lib/config.js
                </span>
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p>FixTheHead &middot; Nefesh Discovery</p>
      <p>
        {hasEmail || hasPhone ? (
          <Fragment>
            {hasEmail && <a href={`mailto:${CONFIG.CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONFIG.CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>}
            {hasEmail && hasPhone && <Fragment> &middot; </Fragment>}
            {hasPhone && <a href={telHref}>{CONFIG.CONTACT_PHONE}</a>}
          </Fragment>
        ) : (
          <span class="placeholder">add CONTACT_EMAIL / CONTACT_PHONE in src/lib/config.js</span>
        )}
      </p>
      <p class="disclaimer">
        Please Note: I am not a licensed therapist, clinical psychologist, or
        medical professional, and my sessions are not medical or mental
        health advice or treatment. Nefesh Discovery is an educational,
        experiential, and spiritual exploration intended to empower your
        personal development and self-inquiry journey.
      </p>
      <p>&copy; {year} FixTheHead. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
